#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

bc_client_t *bc_connect_stdio(const char *const argv[]);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Launches a \f[CR]bash\-server(1)\f[R] subprocess and connects to it via
standard input/output pipes.
The \f[CR]argv\f[R] array specifies the command and arguments to
execute; it must be NULL\-terminated.
.PP
The function forks and executes the specified command using
\f[CR]execvp(3)\f[R], redirecting the child\(cqs stdin and stdout
through a pipe pair.
The child process is expected to speak the bash\-server protocol on its
stdio (i.e., the server should be invoked with \f[CR]\-\-stdio\f[R]).
.PP
This transport mode is useful for:
.IP \(bu 2
Launching a server on demand without a pre\-existing socket.
.IP \(bu 2
Running the server over SSH
(\f[CR]{\(dqssh\(dq, \(dqhost\(dq, \(dqbash\-server\(dq, \(dq\-\-stdio\(dq, NULL}\f[R]).
.IP \(bu 2
Embedding bash\-server in a parent process without socket setup.
.PP
The returned handle must eventually be released with
\f[CR]bc_close(3)\f[R], which also terminates the child subprocess.
