.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The child subprocess is launched via \f[CR]fork(2)\f[R] +
\f[CR]execvp(3)\f[R], so the program in \f[CR]argv[0]\f[R] must be in
\f[CR]$PATH\f[R] or specified as an absolute path.
.IP \(bu 2
When \f[CR]bc_close(3)\f[R] is called, the child process receives
\f[CR]SIGTERM\f[R].
If it does not exit within a short grace period, \f[CR]SIGKILL\f[R] is
sent.
.IP \(bu 2
The stdio transport uses two pipes (one for each direction).
The child\(cqs stderr is inherited from the parent and is not captured
by the client library.
.IP \(bu 2
Authentication is still required after connecting.
The server in \f[CR]\-\-stdio\f[R] mode typically reads the token from
\f[CR]\-\-auth\-fd\f[R] or prints it to stderr on startup.
.IP \(bu 2
Unlike \f[CR]bc_connect(3)\f[R], this function creates a private server
instance.
Multiple calls to \f[CR]bc_connect_stdio\f[R] create independent server
processes.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]argv\f[R] array is not modified or freed by the library.
The caller retains ownership.
